---
/*
  Sprint 2A Feature shell — static reproduction of the immutable golden
  master's Feature ("case file") page (reference/newsstand-original/source/
  Newsstand - Full Site.dc.html, the `isFeature` sc-if block, ~lines
  142-240).

  Content classification (Sprint 2A content-shell rule — see
  DESIGN_DEVIATIONS.md and AGENTS.md):
  - CLASS 1, structural/interface copy (Feature / p.04, figure numbering,
    "The verdict", "The spec", field labels, "Next") is production-final
    visual language.
  - CLASS 2, everything else below (headline, dek, narrative paragraphs,
    pull quote, handwritten notes, build-step prose, statistics, spec
    values, CTA narrative) is source-faithful reference/demo copy carried
    over verbatim to preserve composition and density. None of it is
    verified production content — see the placeholder-claims list in the
    Sprint 2A task contract. It arrives for real in a later content
    checkpoint (Content Collection entry, not this page shell).
  - The Lorem ipsum narrative paragraphs are literal golden-master
    placeholder text, not a Sprint 2A shortcut.
*/
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/feature.css';

const title = 'The inbox that learned to answer itself | CABALLERO!';
const description =
  'Feature / p.04 — the case file behind an AI-and-automation build. Demo content pending final Sprint 2 review.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="feature-page container">
    <header class="feature-head">
      <p class="feature-kicker">Feature / p.04 &middot; AI &amp; Automation</p>
      <h1 class="feature-headline">The inbox that learned to answer itself</h1>
      <p class="feature-dek">
        Nine hundred customer emails a week, three overworked staff, and a brief
        that just said &ldquo;add AI.&rdquo; What we did instead — and why the
        boring version is the one still running.
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-meta">
        <li>Words &amp; build: John Vincent Caballero</li>
        <li>Role: solo — research to deploy</li>
        <li>7 weeks &middot; 2026</li>
        <li>Stack: n8n &middot; TypeScript &middot; Postgres &middot; LLM</li>
      </ul>
    </header>

    <figure class="feature-hero">
      <div class="feature-hero__frame" data-reveal>
        <img
          class="feature-hero__image"
          data-parallax="14"
          src="https://picsum.photos/seed/caballero-hero/1600/700"
          width="1600"
          height="700"
          alt="Placeholder stock photo standing in for the workflow routing canvas — temporary demo image, not a real project screenshot"
